This parameter is required.', example='pc-**************', position='Query'),
  ownerAccount?: string(name='OwnerAccount', position='Query'),
  ownerId?: long(name='OwnerId', position='Query'),
  resourceOwnerAccount?: string(name='ResourceOwnerAccount', position='Query'),
  resourceOwnerId?: long(name='ResourceOwnerId', position='Query'),
  ruleConfig: string(name='RuleConfig', description='The JSON string of the configuration parameters and their values for the SQL throttling rule to be modified. All parameter values are of the string type. Example: `{"id":"test","enabled":"true","match_mode":"0","template":"dXBkYXRlIHQgc2V0IGEgPSAxIHdoZXJlIGlkID0gMQ==","user":"","database":"","waiting":1024,"endpoint":"[{"EndpointName":"pe-***********","EndpointType":"Cluster","DBEndpointDescription":"Cluster Address"}]","throttle_mode":0,"concurrency":1}`. Parameters:
* `"id"`: Required. The name of the throttling rule. The name must meet the following requirements:
  - The name cannot exceed 30 characters in length.
  - The name must consist of uppercase letters, lowercase letters, and digits. Call instructions: Complete sub-parameter documentation: Annotate the type, value range, business meaning, and conditional dependencies for each field, such as the enumeration values and meanings of match_mode, the values and meanings of throttle_mode, the valid ranges of waiting and concurrency, and the conditional requirement rules for endpoint.

This parameter is required.', example='{"id":"test","enabled":"true","match_mode":"0","template":"dXBkYXRlIHQgc2V0IGEgPSAxIHdoZXJlIGlkID0gMQ==","user":"","database":"","waiting":1024,"endpoint":"[{"EndpointName":"pe-***********","EndpointType":"Cluster","DBEndpointDescription":"Cluster Address"}]","throttle_mode":0,"concurrency":1}', position='Query'),
  ruleName: string(name='RuleName', description='The name of the SQL throttling rule. You can specify only one rule name at a time.
> * You can call the [DescribeSQLRateLimitingRules](https://help.aliyun.com/document_detail/212573.html) operation to query the details of all SQL throttling rules in the specified cluster, including the rule names.
> * If the specified rule name does not exist in the current cluster, the system automatically creates a new SQL throttling rule based on the name and the value of `RuleConfig`.

This parameter is required.', example='testrule', position='Query'),
}

